{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQZubKKhNAQEriTXxKhY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Got it. Customers choose, and the options are 2, 3 or 4 equal installments. I've noted that and won't ask about it again. Five decisions are still open. My recommendation is in bold, and you can answer by number and letter, for example \"1a 2a 3a 4a 5a\".\n\n**Settled so far**\n- The customer picks the plan, not billing staff.\n- Plans are 2, 3 or 4 equal installments. No custom schedules.\n- Everything from the last round still holds: integer cents, the 2% fee rate, the 3-day reminder offset, and invoices without a plan behaving as today.\n\n**Mine:** unchanged. One addition: `chooseInstallments(id, count)` rejects any count other than 2, 3 or 4.\n\n**Questions**\n\n1. **When can a customer choose a plan?**\n   - **(a) Only while the invoice is `sent` (not overdue or paid), with nothing paid yet.**\n   - (b) While it's `sent`, even after a partial payment. The remaining balance gets split.\n   - (c) Also when it's overdue, as a way to catch up.\n   - I recommend (a) because it keeps the split simple. (c) would also mean deciding whether a fee already charged gets waived.\n\n2. **When are the installments due?**\n   - **(a) The first on the original due date, then one every month after that.** A 4-part plan ends 3 months later.\n   - (b) Split across the time before the original due date, so the last installment lands on it. The customer gets no extra time.\n   - I recommend (a) because more time to pay is usually why people want installments. (b) keeps your cash flow unchanged.\n\n3. **What happens when one installment is missed?** Same options as before.\n   - **(a) The invoice becomes `overdue`, and only the missed installments are due.**\n   - (b) The invoice becomes `overdue`, and the whole remaining balance is due right away (acceleration).\n   - (c) Nothing happens until the final installment date passes.\n\n4. **Where do payments go?** Same as before.\n   - **(a) To the oldest unpaid installment first. Anything extra goes to the next ones.**\n   - (b) Only to the current installment. Anything extra is held as credit.\n\n5. **How do reminders work?** Same as before.\n   - **(a) A reminder 3 days before each installment.**\n   - (b) Just one reminder, before the final due date.\n\n**Next round, after #3 is answered:** how the late fee applies to a missed installment, and which installment absorbs the leftover cents when the total doesn't divide evenly (for example, $100 in 3 parts)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2460,"cache_read_input_tokens":38639,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2460},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ac170cb-b5f9-41dd-801b-7352604639cd","uuid":"81508b51-6d34-4f9e-a5ed-34746483911e","timestamp":"2026-11-26T00:09:48.993Z","request_id":"req_011ChQZubBsuPGKyH1CuER2F"}
